type="html">Five years into the authoritarian rule of Tunisian President Kais Saied, Human Rights Watch and other activists warn that Tunisia's once vibrant civil society is in danger of being completely stifled.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola caseload tops 6,000 as concerns grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b159f65ace57a8ff417fe8c57819bf0501cd173a945fc4562a47e786ceeb4de0</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447--5f990f71c7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has surpassed 6,000 confirmed cases, with nearly 3,000 deaths. As the virus spreads, authorities are racing to contain one of the deadliest outbreaks in history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's aging autocrats fight to stay in power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c02fe06a7e0a5c5bd31a8c1a157766ed31ace95496181efffe295a36ca4979d</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:12Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-aging-autocrats-fight-to-stay-in-power/a-78487210--45be184aa17e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-aging-autocrats-fight-to-stay-in-power/a-78487210?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As some of Africa's longest-serving leaders grow older, they are using different tactics to extend their rule. But age, succession battles and public pressure pose new challenges.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What does Saxony-Anhalt's election mean for migrants?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b10edc53fbf792b79a0e5e72e3f37f203a5f5826eba95706072f308b80173fe</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:12Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-does-saxony-anhalt-s-election-mean-for-migrants/a-78504553--ae71d2d9cd41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-does-saxony-anhalt-s-election-mean-for-migrants/a-78504553?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD could make history in the German state of Saxony-Anhalt. For many people with a migration background, the September 6 state election raises questions about belonging, security and their future in Germany.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Amanal Petros: From refugee to European champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f6538eb7b83854331338a9752adad5869883d6921e2dc07dc39f80c517ef46b</id><updated>2026-09-02T12:50:12Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504--a9305ea94714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amanal Petros fled the Eritrean–Ethiopian war and came to Germany as a teenager. Now one of the world's top marathon runners, he recently won gold at the European Athletics Championships.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry></feed>
